%% Spoken Pantry Identifier
%% final project: accessible pantry item identifier
%% Does: describe what happens when the program runs, in plain language, with
%%       no file names, no function names and no jargon
%% Does not: describe the code. final_project_ia.mermaid shows where the code
%%       came from, and ARCHITECTURE.md shows which function calls which.
%%       this one is for explaining the thing to somebody who does not code
%% Reasoning: every other diagram in this project answers "how is it built".
%%       none of them answered "what does it actually do", which is the
%%       question anyone asks first. written so it can be read out loud.

flowchart TD
    classDef user fill:#dbeef0,stroke:#0e7c86,stroke-width:2px,color:#0a3f45
    classDef work fill:#f2f5f6,stroke:#5b6b76,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1f2933
    classDef good fill:#dff0e4,stroke:#3f7d5c,stroke-width:2px,color:#1f4a34
    classDef careful fill:#fbe6e3,stroke:#c9483f,stroke-width:2px,color:#8e2f27

    A["you photograph one or more<br/>pantry items on a plain,<br/>dark surface"]:::user
    B["the program looks for the<br/>items in the photo"]:::work
    C["it separates each item<br/>into its own small picture"]:::work
    D{"did it find<br/>anything?"}:::work
    E["it says so out loud, and asks<br/>for a plainer background"]:::careful
    F["for each item it found:<br/>compare against the nine<br/>items it has learned"]:::work
    G{"is it sure<br/>enough?"}:::work
    H["it names the item out loud"]:::good
    I["it says it is not sure, gives<br/>its best guess, and asks you<br/>to double check"]:::careful
    J["every answer ends the same way:<br/>this is a prototype, not a<br/>verified identification"]:::user

    A --> B
    B --> C
    C --> D
    D -- "no" --> E
    D -- "yes" --> F
    F --> G
    G -- "yes" --> H
    G -- "no" --> I
    H --> J
    I --> J

    subgraph LEARNED["what it learned from, once, before any of this"]
        direction LR
        K["photos of the nine items,<br/>taken by hand"]:::user
        L["each photo trimmed down<br/>to just the item"]:::work
        M["it studies those trimmed<br/>photos and remembers what<br/>each item looks like"]:::work
        K --> L --> M
    end

    M -. "this is the memory<br/>the comparison uses" .-> F
